  "what_this_declares": "The exact set of unit ids whose DONE_RUNG_STAMP status the B18 regeneration supersedes. Every one is a class_feature that moved sheet-complete -> text-complete. Both statuses are DONE; text-complete sits ABOVE the sheet-complete rung on the ladder (SHEET_COMPLETE_PROMOTABLE_STATUSES' own doc comment: 'grounded, text-complete and the oracle dispositions sit ABOVE it and keep their own word -- they are already terminal'), so this is a relabel UPWARD, not a completion loss. Corpus completion is unchanged by it.",
  "cause": "class_feature_pool_catalog_holds() now returns true for these records, so classify() returns text-complete (evidence class_feature_pool_catalog_serves_a_rendered_description) instead of engine-does-not-hold; text-complete is not in SHEET_COMPLETE_PROMOTABLE_STATUSES, so the sheet-complete rung no longer promotes them. The committed inventory predates that catalog widening.",
  "pre_existing": "Not caused by ruling B18. The identical 230 stamps, the same first offenders and the same 'stamped 23085 unit(s) (dice=911, number=4768, words=17406)' rung line are recorded at cycle 14's HEAD in artifacts/epic-6-pcgen-exit/AT-35-E6-003-RULED_cycle15_receipt.md. No cycle since has been able to regenerate docs/work-inventory.json because of it.",
  "not_allow_stamp_loss": "--allow-stamp-loss would also wave through the 7,615-stamp regression the guard exists to stop (measured: run without CORPUS_LITERAL_SWEEP_REPORT/DERIVED_FIXTURE_CHECK_REPORT). This declaration is an EQUALITY: one undeclared loss refuses the write.",
  "status_moves": {
    "sheet-complete -> text-complete": 230
  },
  "count": 230,
  "re_derive": "CORPUS_LITERAL_SWEEP_REPORT=<sweep --json-out> DERIVED_FIXTURE_CHECK_REPORT=<fixture --json-out> cargo run --locked --release --bin v06_work_inventory -- --stdout-only > /tmp/wi-new.json, then diff the DONE_RUNG_STAMP_STATUSES id sets of docs/work-inventory.json and /tmp/wi-new.json",
